{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/909003-homebrew-medicine-charms","id":909003,"title":"[Homebrew] Medicine Charms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-07T02:37:23-07:00","id":909003,"title":"[Homebrew] Medicine Charms","content":"I quite like the Medicine tree as it stands. PCC excepted. But it's short, and I think it could use a bit more meat. So...<br /> <br /> <b>Blessed Regime Instruction</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Simple (Instant)<br /> Prereqs: Medicine 4, Essence 1<br /> <br /> Those who listen to the words of the Solar doctor need never know illness or insanity.<br /> <br /> The Solar spends an hour talking to someone (possibly herself) about their physical and mental health, listening to their problems and giving them advice for addressing them. Unless subject to plague, poison, serious trauma, or hostile magic, a patient who follows the Solar's instructions will enjoy good physical and mental health for the next month. The ordinary stresses and illnesses of life simply will not affect them. If they wish to gain or lose weight, they will be able to. If they are pregnant, their child will be healthy and their birth easy. If they're not truly infertile, they will have full control over whether they conceive children.<br /> <br /> In addition, the Solar's advice invigorates her patient. They will never fail to follow their instructions through mere laziness or forgetfulness during the following month.<br /> <br /> <b>Malady-Detecting Instinct</b><br /> Cost: 1m; Reflexive (Instant)<br /> Prereqs: Medicine 4, Essence 2, Flawless Diagnosis Technique<br /> <br /> When a Solar doctor applies their god-given power, internal bleeding and hallucinations seem as obvious as a severed arm.<br /> <br /> This Charm may be activated at any time. It allows the Solar to perform an instantaneous diagnosis attempt, simply by looking at her patient.<br /> <br /> <b>Spider Doctor Training Technique</b><br /> Cost: 10m, 1wp; Simple (Instant)<br /> Prereqs: Medicine 5, Essence 2, Blessed Regime Instruction<br /> <br /> Just as the Bronze Tigers train tiger warriors, the Copper Spiders train spider doctors.<br /> <br /> The Solar spends a day or a month instructing other doctors and teaching them about medicine. In a day, the Solar can give her audience a +2 bonus to treat a specific disease or other problem. The bonus lasts for a month, and negates penalties for being untrained. In a month, the Solar can give each member of her audience two additional dots of Medicine and any number of Medicine specialties that she possesses. They must spend experience normally if they track it, and may not increase their Medicine score this way more than once.<br /> <br /> <b>Solar Apothecary Practice</b><br /> Cost: 4m; Simple (Indefinite)<br /> Prereqs: Medicine 5, Essence 3, Contagion-Curing Touch<br /> <br /> Mortal medicine may be the difference between life and death for those who fall victim to poison and disease. But compared to the medicines of the Sun, it is a sad and petty thing.<br /> <br /> The Solar spends an hour mixing a medicine, and rolls to treat a specific disease or poison. Her attempt is contained within the medicine, and as long as she keeps her motes committed anyone who takes the medicine benefits as though she'd treated him directly. The treatment attempt may be enhanced with other Charms; for example, Instant Treatment Methodology may be used to instantly make medicine that takes effect instantly.<br /> <br /> <b>A Hood On Death</b><br /> Cost: 15m, 1wp; Simple (Until research is complete)<br /> Prereqs: Medicine 5, Essence 4, Solar Apothecary Practice, Spider-Doctor Training Technique<br /> <br /> Long ago, when the Solar Exalted ruled the world, many diseases were removed from existence entirely. To this day, the world is blessed by the absence of atravia and waterpox and shepherd's rot. But with time new plagues have arisen, and new remedies must be sought.<br /> <br /> This Charm is an extended action in which the Solar seeks to create a formula for a medicine to treat a specific poison or disease. The difficulty is the difficulty to treat the poison or resist the disease. The terminus starts at 1, and may be increased in the following ways:<br /> <br /> +1 if the Solar makes the formula complex enough that only a competent doctor can make the medicine<br /> +2 if only a master doctor can make the medicine<br /> +3 if only a supernaturally excellent doctor can make the medicine<br /> +1 if the medicine requires medicinal herbs or other ingredients that are not trivial to come by<br /> +2 if the medicine requires truly rare or expensive ingredients<br /> +1 if the Solar has other doctors to help them design the medicine<br /> +1 if the Solar has some test subjects to work with<br /> <br /> The interval depends on the severity of the malady. A week for something ordinary like a flu or snake venom. A month for something deadly like smallpox or Yozi venom. A season for something truly terrible like the Great Contagion or the concentrated hatred of Kimbery. Regardless, the task demands roughly eight hours a day. The work may be set aside without loss of progress.<br /> <br /> The action has no fixed goal number. 15 successes suffice to create a medicine that counts as a superior tool, like the best mundane medicines. 30 successes suffice to create a medicine that adds two automatic successes to all relevant rolls. 45 successes suffices to create a medicine that cures the recipient infallibly. 60 successes suffices to create a medicine that cures the recipient and makes them permanently immune to that poison or disease.<br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b><br /> <br /> Main inspiration for these is the manga Jin.<br /> <br /> Blessed Regime Instruction is heavily inspired by Shyft's work over on SV. If what I've heard from doctors is to be believed, the &quot;patient will not be lazy or forgetful&quot; bit would be incredibly useful in real life. The fertility stuff is in there to give it a more old-world-myth feel.<br /> <br /> Malady-Detecting Insight was originally gonna be like Watchman's Infallible Eye, a Permanent Charm that tells you when you should diagnose someone. But I like this better.<br /> <br /> Spider Doctor Training Technique doesn't provide nearly as dramatic a bonus as Tiger Warrior Training Technique does. I hope it's still useful. And yes, I know the name is silly. But I like it.<br /> <br /> Dreams of the First Age gets a lot of hate and deserves most of it. But when I wanted to write up a Solar medicine-making Charm, it was useful. I didn't keep the multi-target nature of the original, though.<br /> <br /> A Hood On Death is the Charm I'm proudest of here. Everyone wants to be Jonas Salk, right? And I like the way it shapes plague-fighting narratives. It lets you perform medicine on a grand scale, without rendering other doctors unnecessary or making the story boring. Spreading your new medicine is still a challenge. My only regrets are that it's complicated, and that I'm really not sure about those goal numbers.<br /> <br /> This will be my last batch of Charms for a while. I feel like I've got the Solar Charmset in a shape I like, now. Or I will once I've done a bit more editing. So I won't be writing anything more until and unless inspiration strikes or a need arises.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":1154,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","user":"Sanctaphrax","date":". 06-08-2016, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T15:40:50-07:00","id":910374,"title":"","content":"Blessed Regime Instruction is pretty neat. I'd move the &quot;doesn't protect&quot; clause into the main text, like thus:<br /> <br /> &quot;Unless subject to plague, poisoning, serious trauma or other magic, a patient who follows the Solar's instructions will enjoy good physical and mental health for the next month.&quot;<br /> <br /> Malady-Detecting Instinct looks good.<br /> <br /> I think I mentioned that in my thread that I don't like charms like Spider Doctor Training Technique. But if you do, I might change the long version to &quot;With a month, each student increases his medicine rating to 3 if it's lower and learns a single Medicine specialty the Solar possesses.&quot; Removes the need for a separate &quot;can't be reused&quot; clause, and I prefer just teaching one specialty vs. any number.<br /> <br /> Solar Apothecary Practice is excellent. I don't like allowing the treatment to contain other charms, though - then you can <i>literally </i>make a potion of Cure Light Wounds. It's a change in intentions, but I'd make it Simple (Instant) and just let it store a Medicine roll.<br /> <br /> I really, really don't like A Hood on Death. It doesn't <i>shape </i>plague-fighting narratives, it <i>removes </i>one of the most interesting / varied elements from them and replaces it with an extended roll. It's a 2e &quot;my very presence warps the setting&quot; style effect, which is otherwise almost completely absent from the charmset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T19:11:54-07:00","id":910478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueWinds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/909003-homebrew-medicine-charms?p=910374#post910374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blessed Regime Instruction is pretty neat. I'd move the &quot;doesn't protect&quot; clause into the main text, like thus:<br /> <br /> &quot;Unless subject to plague, poisoning, serious trauma or other magic, a patient who follows the Solar's instructions will enjoy good physical and mental health for the next month.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Good idea. Will do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueWinds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/909003-homebrew-medicine-charms?p=910374#post910374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I mentioned that in my thread that I don't like charms like Spider Doctor Training Technique. But if you do, I might change the long version to &quot;With a month, each student increases his medicine rating to 3 if it's lower and learns a single Medicine specialty the Solar possesses.&quot; Removes the need for a separate &quot;can't be reused&quot; clause, and I prefer just teaching one specialty vs. any number.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like it to be possible to make a skilled doctor even better with this. That way you have an incentive to work with existing experts, rather than random scrubs.<br /> <br /> Might go down to one specialty, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueWinds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/909003-homebrew-medicine-charms?p=910374#post910374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solar Apothecary Practice is excellent. I don't like allowing the treatment to contain other charms, though - then you can <i>literally </i>make a potion of Cure Light Wounds. It's a change in intentions, but I'd make it Simple (Instant) and just let it store a Medicine roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure if that would be useful enough. Even as-is, there's not a lot of reason to use the Charm unless the person you want to treat is hard for you to get to.<br /> <br /> And anyway I'm fine with potions of Cure Light Wounds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueWinds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/909003-homebrew-medicine-charms?p=910374#post910374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really, really don't like A Hood on Death. It doesn't <i>shape </i>plague-fighting narratives, it <i>removes </i>one of the most interesting / varied elements from them and replaces it with an extended roll. It's a 2e &quot;my very presence warps the setting&quot; style effect, which is otherwise almost completely absent from the charmset.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean by removing one of the most interesting elements from a plague-fighting narrative?<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, finding cures and vaccines consists of (the equivalent of) an extended roll if you can do it. Which you generally can't, in pre-modern times. If smallpox was devastating Exalted North America, and an Exalted medicine man without a Charm like this wanted to find a cure, I'd probably just tell them no. You can treat people one-on-one, but creating an bottled cure that mortals can manufacture is just not on.<br /> <br /> As for warping the setting, I don't think it's much different from the ability to make high-level Artifacts. But I guess you want to keep that in check too...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T23:31:06-07:00","id":910598,"title":"","content":"We've argued over this a lot in my rewrite, so I thought I'd try and clear it up a little, since it feels like we're talking past each other. I want <i>characters </i>to make high level artifacts - I don't want <i>charms </i>to do so. Does that distinction make sense?<br /> <br /> Basically, it's always easy for a ST to gloss over something they're not interested in with a single (extended?) roll - but once the rules reduce something to that by default (even in the text of a charm characters won't always have), it's very, very hard to draw it back out again.<br /> <br /> Again, it's not about having weaker characters or weaker charms, it's about retaining the story and wonder and entertainment value around things. Collapsing stories down into dice rolls is easy (Bureaucracy is king in this regard), and turning simple dice rolls back into extended stories is hard (&quot;didn't we resolve this with a roll last week?&quot; or &quot;hey, I have a charm that solves this, why are we going to talk to that god again?&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T14:59:48-07:00","id":911173,"title":"","content":"I think I understand your position. And I actually agree with it for the most part.<br /> <br /> The difference in our stances, I think, is that I believe there are some problems that <i>should</i> be collapsed into rolls. Creating a medicine is a great example; it's an important process but it's also super boring if you're not a specialist in the field. What Jonas Salk actually did, for the most part, was sit in a lab doing medical work all day every day for years. That's exactly the kind of task that ought to be turned into an extended roll, because it's just not very fun to play out.<br /> <br /> Funding and distributing the medicine when it's done, meanwhile, can be quite a story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T20:18:25-07:00","id":913829,"title":"","content":"So, anyone have any further comments before I finalize these?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T06:43:22-07:00","id":1336195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/909003-homebrew-medicine-charms?p=913829#post913829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, anyone have any further comments before I finalize these?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, yes. <br /> <br /> So for 'A hood on death', what about something like regeneration? How would, in the modern day, techniques to regrow organs and limbs be counted as? What about something like HIV or AIDs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T07:27:00-07:00","id":1336206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/909003-homebrew-medicine-charms?p=1336195#post1336195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, yes.<br /> <br /> So for 'A hood on death', what about something like regeneration? How would, in the modern day, techniques to regrow organs and limbs be counted as? What about something like HIV or AIDs?</div> </div> </div> </div>The comment you are replying to is over 3 years old, and from a poster who was banned more than 1 year ago. I think it's safe to say you won't be getting an answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 09-17-2019, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T07:46:15-07:00","id":1336209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/909003-homebrew-medicine-charms?p=1336206#post1336206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The comment you are replying to is over 3 years old, and from a poster who was banned more than 1 year ago. I think it's safe to say you won't be getting an answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. Wow. Well, I'll deal with it on my own, then. <br /> <br /> Anyone in contact with him? I want to use his homebrew.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}